CredLens migrations use DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED from the process environment or the
root .env/.env.local. Never put credentials in alembic.ini.

From backend/: .venv/bin/python -m alembic upgrade head
Check metadata: .venv/bin/python -m alembic check
Generate changes: .venv/bin/python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m 'description'
Review every generated migration. Test upgrade/downgrade on a disposable Neon
branch first; downgrade drops data and is not a routine production rollback.
